  "details": "This is old request, and some people want save pins too due their reasons. Especially as streamer, you have mostly same pin setups all the time.\n\nIt's good idea to make pins save permanent so it will stored and can loaded again by next game start.\n\nReset can done with a extra button near pins as reset button.\n\nSecond, pin rotation is still weird because it's always between 2 pins. Some players want just close camera options menu and use hand to rotate easy through all 3 pins. So why not make full pin rotation?\n\nThird, the follow player option (look at function) only works in landscape, and if you put it up as portrait, it will rotate back to landscape.\n\nMight add toggle for portrait/landscape position of the camera. This should also stored in pin.\n\nIt's because part of streamers always set it as portrait.",
